{"title":"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be an injective function from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06cc90a55154119e08022c416832b4981fe19975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1,2,3,\\ldots}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> in itself. Prove that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb4ec92fd3acf0b7b5eb976ace404d2e070f419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{n} f(k)k^{-2} \\geq \\sum_{k=1}^{n} k^{-1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"176\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that all the unknowns are integers, so the smallest one must greater or equal to 1.\n</p><p>Let me denote the permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/02118c4a58fae9098a23563b722303b87f566f56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k_1,k_2,...,k_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/26128e25236a40f7789fa397c0d83c93846d584f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y_1,y_2,...,y_n)=y_i (*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>From the rearrangement's inequality we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc64ed2c69841f5a9d63c094d02becb71128707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Random Sum} \\geq \\text{Reversed Sum}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"225\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We will denote we permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6ceb79ebc4bf613298e0144eae25dd73de9be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> in this form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de865c023d2b61fda6a653a4333f92501d0b287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_n \\geq ...\\geq y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>So we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3ffd42b113b69981a32ac2c574a497fbad4f743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k_1}{1^2}+\\frac{k_2}{2^2}+...+\\frac{k_n}{n^2} \\geq \\frac{y_1}{1^2}+ \\frac{y_2}{2^2}+...+ \\frac{y_n}{n^2} \\geq 1+\\frac{1}{2}+...+\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"457\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Let's denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3d1c036920e9075d390d3b64eae90619dfd134.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y_1}{1^2}+ \\frac{y_2}{2^2}+...+ \\frac{y_n}{n^2}=T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"182\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a828fdd51f4806a937e63a1885b450398c5e5486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\frac{1}{2}+...+\\frac{1}{n}=S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/5/d452244295cecc510d85cebd3dd9528ba8bded5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T \\geq S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />. Which comes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c46a508bb0ea661c24ac8b5f4cf7455965a326d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1 \\geq1, y_2 \\geq2, ...,y_n \\geq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>So we are done.\n</p><p>The above solution was posted and copyrighted by Davron. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p509573\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(Note, the official problem statement is much nicer, so we will go by that&#160;:&gt;)\n</p><p><b>Problem Statement:</b>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d1429906e4a890eced37ef00d03d91ea4eb4ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"11\" /> be distinct positive integers. Prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/8/b68bfdb07e173249c1b617a55c7c7eb0a7f612e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x_1}{1^2} + \\dots + \\frac{x_n}{n^2} \\geq \\frac{1}{1} + \\frac{1}{2} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{n}\\]\" width=\"260\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof</b>:\n</p><p>We prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/40786665d1be70fb50c4a71b32d2c0a6c83ed936.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x_1}{1^2} + \\frac{x_2}{2^2} + \\dots + \\frac{x_n}{n^2} \\geq H_n\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5f39a6a69f2685703aae3fb9f9137fedc6b85c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> is the harmonic series. \n</p><p>By the rearrangement inequality, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> denotes the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2189db2b3db7251d01e0070bb4225533df1ef17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" /> on the LHS and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a936caf3cc80ede995875ddf4da3138dabb29b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12dcbe43da89be946383ccb550f54cfe5d970532.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{1 \\leq i \\leq n} \\frac{x_i}{i^2} \\geq \\sum_{1 \\leq i \\leq n} \\frac{a_i}{i^2}\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>It is sufficient to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281f36d337865598d23476fe7b13e65b3dfdf365.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_i}{i^2} \\geq H_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p><b>Lemma:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8282208e9775909a5aa674151639ae3a2a279d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\geq i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><b>Proof of the Lemma:</b>\n</p><p>Arrange <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> increasingly from which, for the sake of contradiction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb457628a9dab48eb82e28154046cfd2c3e25b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &lt; i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />, then it follows that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> must be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. The elements are distinct however so by the Pigeonhole Principle one number cannot be fulfilled hence a contradiction, as desired.\n</p><p><b>1978 IMO/Q5:</b>\n</p><p>It follows that by the <b>Lemma</b> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b2feb838e2a6b919e8052d63386b87540c1196d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_i}{i^2} \\geq \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{1}{k}\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"48\" />. \n</p><p>The RHS however is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5f39a6a69f2685703aae3fb9f9137fedc6b85c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO\" title=\"1978 IMO\">1978 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1978 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017162801\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 162/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6399/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.684      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    8.684      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19714:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017162801 and revision id 287606. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}